WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.280
The "G.I. Joe" movie franchise has been missing in&nbsp;
action, but if there's one guy who can rescue it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:10.160
it's the ninja known as Snake Eyes. The character&nbsp;
is returning in an all-new series reboot;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:13.760
here's everything you need to know&nbsp;
about "Snake Eyes: G.I. Joe Origins."

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.720
The first bit of news about the "Snake&nbsp;
Eyes" movie that the public heard came&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.920
out over three years ago, way back in May 2018.

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:23.840
At the time, the Hollywood Reporter confirmed&nbsp;
that Paramount Pictures had put into development&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:28.160
a "G.I. Joe" spin-off film centered around Snake&nbsp;
Eyes, tapping the live-action "Beauty and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.160 --> 00:00:33.040
Beast" movie screenwriter Evan Spiliotopoulos&nbsp;
to pen the script and Brian Goldner to produce.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:37.440
The outlet also noted that executives at&nbsp;
Paramount and Hasbro had been keen on rebooting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:41.600
the "G.I. Joe" franchise, and had commissioned a&nbsp;
writers room dedicated to developing movies and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:46.480
cinematic universes around the Hasbro properties,&nbsp;
including "G.I. Joe," "Transformers," "M.A.S.K.",&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.400
and "Micronauts." By all accounts, the&nbsp;
"Snake Eyes" solo flick was one such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:55.120
idea - and according to an interview producer&nbsp;
Lorenzo di Bonaventura gave to Entertainment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.120 --> 00:01:00.240
Weekly in 2021, it was one of the only solid&nbsp;
ideas that writers room happened to produce.

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:04.800
Things were relatively quiet on the&nbsp;
"Snake Eyes" front until December 2018,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:08.320
when Robert Schwentke signed on as&nbsp;
the film's director. Audiences will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.320 --> 00:01:11.520
know Schwentke as the director behind&nbsp;
movies like "The Time Traveler's Wife,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.840
"R.I.P.D.," "The Divergent Series: Insurgent,"&nbsp;
and "The Divergent Series: Allegiant."

00:01:15.840 --> 00:01:21.200
In 2010's "G.I. Joe: The Rise of Cobra" and&nbsp;
2013's "G.I. Joe: Retaliation," the Scottish&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:26.480
martial artist Ray Park played Snake Eyes. In&nbsp;
December 2018, "G.I. Joe" franchise producer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.480 --> 00:01:31.120
Lorenzo di Bonaventura confirmed with Slashfilm&nbsp;
that Ray Park wouldn't be reprising his role&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.120 --> 00:01:35.200
for the character's origin story, leaving&nbsp;
the possibilities for the movie wide open.

00:01:35.200 --> 00:01:40.080
It wasn't until mid-2019 that the "Snake Eyes:&nbsp;
G.I. Joe Origins" cast started to come together,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.040
and a few more months after that&nbsp;
before the movie kicked off production.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:49.040
So, if Ray Park isn't Snake Eyes, then who is?&nbsp;
That'd be Malaysian English actor Henry Golding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:53.120
whose performance as Nick Young in the beloved&nbsp;
romantic comedy "Crazy Rich Asians" has led&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:57.680
to roles in the feature films "A Simple Favor,"&nbsp;
"Monsoon," "Last Christmas," and "The Gentlemen."

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.280
Through "Snake Eyes: G.I. Joe Origins," the&nbsp;
talented actor will be taking on his first&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:01.280 --> 00:02:05.520
leading role in an action movie, and he has&nbsp;
a heck of a supporting cast surrounding him.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:09.760
"Snake Eyes" also stars "Ready or Not" and "Bill&nbsp;
&amp; Ted Face the Music" actress Samara Weaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.760 --> 00:02:14.800
as Scarlett, a fierce G.I. Joe agent who also&nbsp;
works for Clan Arashikage; "Money Heist" star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.800 --> 00:02:19.760
Úrsula Corberó as the Baroness, a member of the&nbsp;
terrorist organization Cobra; Peter Mensah of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.760 --> 00:02:24.960
"Marvel's Agents of S.H.I.E.L.D." fame as Clan&nbsp;
Arashikage's co-leader Blind Master; Andrew Koji&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:29.600
of the excellent Cinemax series "Warrior" as Snake&nbsp;
Eyes' friend-turned-deadly-nemesis Storm Shadow;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:35.920
and Haruka Abe as Akiko, a Clan Arashikage trainee&nbsp;
with connections to Snake Eyes and Storm Shadow.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:40.320
Rounding out the cast of "Snake Eyes" are Iko&nbsp;
Uwais as Storm Shadow's uncle Hard Master,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:44.720
who leads Clan Arashikage; Takehiro&nbsp;
Hira as Cobra member Kenta;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:47.040
and Steven Allerick as Snake Eyes' father.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:51.920
Playing a character as famous as Snake Eyes&nbsp;
in a franchise as action-heavy as "G.I. Joe"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:56.160
would require even in-shape actors to get&nbsp;
more ripped in preparation. Henry Golding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:00.480
whom no one would consider unmuscular in his&nbsp;
everyday life, got totally shredded to play Snake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.680
Eyes - undergoing intense training that yielded&nbsp;
impressive results. In November 2020, Golding&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:09.920
said that he "became a weapon" during "Snake&nbsp;
Eyes: G.I. Joe Origins" prep, and even shared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.840
a jaw-dropping clip from one of his training&nbsp;
sessions on The Tonight Show with Jimmy Fallon.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.600
"It put me through my paces. We had,&nbsp;
like, four hours of choreography&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:21.520
every single day. We had two hours of&nbsp;
script work, then like an hour of PT."

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:25.920
According to Golding, the producers of "Snake&nbsp;
Eyes" went out on a limb in casting him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:29.120
having faith that he would be able to build&nbsp;
on his boxing and martial arts background&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:33.120
to become a credible supersoldier. That&nbsp;
bet seems to have paid off in a big way.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.720
"It was worth it, because I became&nbsp;
a weapon, I'm not going to lie."

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:42.080
The "Snake Eyes: G.I. Joe Origins" cast&nbsp;
and crew began filming in October 2019,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:45.360
shooting in Vancouver, Canada from&nbsp;
the 15th of that month to the 9th of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:50.480
December. When Vancouver shooting wrapped, the&nbsp;
production moved to a new locale: Tokyo, Japan.

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:55.360
The cast and crew spent about six weeks in Japan,&nbsp;
and in late February 2020, Golding announced that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.360 --> 00:04:00.080
all principal photography for "Snake Eyes"&nbsp;
was complete, writing in an Instagram post,

00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:03.440
"...and THAT, is a principal wrap&nbsp;
on Snake Eyes lady's and gents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:03.440 --> 00:04:07.920
What a crew we had, Vancouver + Japan, you&nbsp;
were unstoppable. Thank you for the dedication,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:10.480
this film is going to blow&nbsp;
everyone's socks off x."

00:04:10.480 --> 00:04:14.320
Initially, "Snake Eyes" was slated&nbsp;
for a theatrical release on March 27,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.320
2020. Like many movies originally slated for&nbsp;
that year, it ended up going through some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:23.360
release date reshuffling, eventually being taken&nbsp;
off of Paramount's release schedule entirely.

00:04:23.360 --> 00:04:28.160
Over a year later, in March 2021, Golding came&nbsp;
forward with another announcement about filming:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:30.240
"Snake Eyes" was undergoing reshoots.

00:04:30.240 --> 00:04:34.640
In an Instagram post about the reshoots, Golding&nbsp;
acknowledged the difficulty of filming under COVID&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:38.480
protocols, and expressed his happiness that they&nbsp;
were still able to pull it off in spite of it.

00:04:39.120 --> 00:04:43.680
"We just got some reshoots for 'Snake Eyes,' but&nbsp;
I'm so grateful that we're able to pull this off."

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:45.920
After those last minute reshoots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:45.920 --> 00:04:50.240
the film is now officially set to&nbsp;
land in theaters on July 23, 2021.

00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:54.640
First and foremost, "Snake Eyes" will be&nbsp;
an origin story - and as such, fans will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:59.040
get to see the events that transform him into&nbsp;
the masked, silent badass they know and love.

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:03.360
In the "G.I. Joe" animated series and in the&nbsp;
Marvel comics, Snake Eyes' silence has been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:07.440
chalked up to damaged vocal cords, but that&nbsp;
fact was retconned for the feature films.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:07.440 --> 00:05:11.120
Snake Eyes doesn't say a word in "G.I.&nbsp;
Joe: The Rise of Cobra" and "G.I. Joe:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.120 --> 00:05:14.720
Retaliation" because he previously took&nbsp;
a vow of silence following the apparent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:17.440
murder of one of his masters&nbsp;
at the hands of Storm Shadow.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:21.280
The film's story will focus on Snake Eyes&nbsp;
accepting an invitation to begin training&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:26.000
with the Arashikage, a clan of Japanese ninja.&nbsp;
The process will prove more difficult than&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.760
anyone bargained for, as the truth about&nbsp;
Snake Eyes' past comes to the surface,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:33.040
his mind and heart are tested, and&nbsp;
his body is pushed to its limits.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.920
Of course, with Storm Shadow as a&nbsp;
key member of the character roster,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.920 --> 00:05:40.080
there should be an epic showdown between the&nbsp;
dangerous man and his former friend Snake Eyes.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:42.960
Remarks that star Henry Golding&nbsp;
has made indicate that "Snake Eyes"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.880
will be charged with a weighty task:&nbsp;
rebooting the entire "G.I. Joe" film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.880 --> 00:05:50.800
series. During a press conference&nbsp;
in January 2020, the actor said,

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:54.800
"[The movie is] unlike anything people will&nbsp;
have seen. We're really starting a new timeline,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:58.000
a new franchise with[in] the 'G.I.&nbsp;
Joe' universe. To kick it off with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:02.880
such a distinct and stylized film, I think, it&nbsp;
really sets the precedent for follow-up movies."

00:06:02.880 --> 00:06:07.040
While one could make the case that Paramount&nbsp;
and Hasbro are jumping the gun by rebooting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:11.440
the series after only two films, it seems like&nbsp;
a smart move. "G.I. Joe" has the potential to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:14.960
be a smash-hit property along the lines&nbsp;
of the "Fast and Furious" and "Mission:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.960 --> 00:06:18.880
Impossible" franchises, but it hasn't&nbsp;
happened yet; previous entries in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:23.360
franchise, "Rise of Cobra" and "Retaliation"&nbsp;
underperformed critically and commercially.

00:06:23.360 --> 00:06:27.760
In his past comments, Golding perhaps&nbsp;
inadvertently pinned down one big reason for this:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.760 --> 00:06:32.320
a lack of personality. "Snake Eyes" can&nbsp;
fix that, reintroducing the franchise by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:35.440
way of an origin flick for its most&nbsp;
compelling and unique character.

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:41.120
Though "Snake Eyes: G.I. Joe Origins" has yet to&nbsp;
open in theaters, Paramount and Hasbro executives&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.120 --> 00:06:45.600
already have a sequel in the works. The Hollywood&nbsp;
Reporter broke the news in an exclusive report&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:45.600 --> 00:06:50.000
on May 1, 2020, detailing that "Rebecca"&nbsp;
and "Seberg" writers Joe Shrapnel and Anna&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:50.000 --> 00:06:54.240
Waterhouse teamed up to co-write the script&nbsp;
for "Snake Eyes 2." Lorenzo di Bonaventura&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.240 --> 00:06:58.960
is returning to produce and, of course, Henry&nbsp;
Golding is circling back to star as Snake Eyes.

00:06:58.960 --> 00:07:02.560
There isn't a whole lot of information about&nbsp;
the "Snake Eyes" sequel out there just yet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.560 --> 00:07:06.160
and fans will have to wait to see the first&nbsp;
flick to know what might happen in the second.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:09.680
It stands to reason that "Snake Eyes:&nbsp;
G.I. Joe Origins" could end with its&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:09.680 --> 00:07:14.000
eponymous character taking a vow of silence&nbsp;
or venturing to never show his face again,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.000 --> 00:07:18.720
although doing both, while canonically accurate,&nbsp;
might make for an underwhelming follow-up film.

00:07:18.720 --> 00:07:22.640
Lucasfilm's Disney+ streaming series "The&nbsp;
Mandalorian" proved that a project's main&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:22.640 --> 00:07:26.480
character doesn't have to show their face&nbsp;
at all times - Pedro Pascal's Din Djarin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:29.920
almost never takes his helmet off - but that&nbsp;
they should at least speak up every now and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:33.680
then to keep things interesting. There's also&nbsp;
bonus points of course for the masked character&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:33.680 --> 00:07:37.840
showing some wit and humor when they do engage&nbsp;
in conversation. How will fans feel if Snake&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:42.560
Eyes hides his face but not his voice, or vice&nbsp;
versa, instead of doing both down the line?

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:45.840
In any case, it says a lot that&nbsp;
Paramount and Hasbro greenlit a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:49.680
sequel well before "Snake Eyes" debuted.&nbsp;
Fingers crossed that when "Snake Eyes:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:53.760
G.I. Joe Origins" debuts on July&nbsp;
23, it'll blow everyone away.

